1
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,000
BONUS, FIRST NUCLEAR POWER PLANT IN THE TROPICS.

2
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:48,000
BONUS, FOR BOILING WATER NUCLEAR SUPERHEAT,

3
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,000
IS ONE OF THE ATOMIC ENERGY COMMISSION'S

4
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,000
POWER DEMONSTRATION PROJECTS.

5
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:07,000
With its superheat core, it represents one advanced step in AEC's program for the development

6
00:02:10,159 --> 00:02:17,159
of power reactors. And AEC is meeting three-quarters of the total cost of about $24 million.

7
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:33,860
Surrounded by the complex plumbing of nuclear technology,

8
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:38,159
silent and clean as no conventional power plant has ever been,

9
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:47,699
the new reactor will supply superheated steam to a turbo generator designed to produce about 17 megawatts of electricity.

10
00:02:50,099 --> 00:02:53,920
A continuous supply of baseload power.

11
00:02:53,920 --> 00:03:04,040
Although BONUS is not a large plant, as nuclear power reactors go, it forms part of an ambitious

12
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:14,860
plan to supply this island with the power its blooming economy needs.

13
00:03:14,860 --> 00:03:19,440
BONUS will join the conventional generating facilities of the Puerto Rico Water Resources

14
00:03:19,439 --> 00:03:28,199
Authority, co-sponsor of the reactor project. A power grid built up largely during the past

15
00:03:28,199 --> 00:03:37,919
25 years, a foundation for the industrial development of the island. And so in 1960,

16
00:03:37,919 --> 00:03:43,939
the interests of the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico and the United States Atomic Energy Commission

17
00:03:43,939 --> 00:03:47,960
converged on this lonely headland of Punta Iguera.

18
00:03:56,419 --> 00:03:58,960
The work of clearing the site began.

19
00:04:43,939 --> 00:04:55,199
To the formal groundbreaking ceremony came those concerned with the future of this commonwealth

20
00:04:55,199 --> 00:05:01,000
and with progress in the peaceful uses of nuclear energy.

21
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:16,120
like Governor Munoz Mari and Rafael Urrutia of the Water Resources Authority, Congressman

22
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:24,180
Chet Holofield of the Joint Committee on Atomic Energy.

23
00:05:24,180 --> 00:05:29,560
Together they moved the first symbolic shovelful of Earth,

24
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:32,959
a token of the joint effort that would unite Americans

25
00:05:32,959 --> 00:05:38,120
of the island and the mainland in the months ahead.

26
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:42,160
Corbonus is being created through an interlocking pattern of cooperation.

27
00:05:45,220 --> 00:05:49,360
AEC is responsible for and will own the nuclear portion

28
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:52,460
of the plant.

29
00:05:52,459 --> 00:05:58,579
The Water Resources Authority will provide the turbo generator and other conventional facilities required,

30
00:05:58,579 --> 00:06:01,620
and will operate the entire plant.

31
00:06:05,519 --> 00:06:09,899
In turn, AEC has contracted with the Maxson Construction Company,

32
00:06:09,899 --> 00:06:16,199
working from designs prepared by Combustion Engineering Incorporated and Jackson and Moreland.

33
00:06:22,460 --> 00:06:36,620
At the same time, far from this site of Punta Iguera, other elements of BONUS are beginning

34
00:06:36,620 --> 00:06:39,560
to materialize.

35
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:44,360
At the Pacific Coast Engineering Company's plant in California, the reactor's pressure

36
00:06:44,360 --> 00:06:46,680
vessel takes form.

37
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:52,040
This is one of the most critical components of the reactor, and it's certainly the biggest.

38
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:30,080
welding and drilling, its 61 tons are shaped to the most exacting standards of integrity.

39
00:07:30,080 --> 00:07:36,500
For this vessel must contain the reactor core, the nuclear furnace, a tempest of boiling

40
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:45,560
water and superheated steam. The fundamental achievement of the atomic age, a controlled

41
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:52,120
nuclear chain reaction is put to work in the power reactor.

42
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:55,560
The heat energy of the fission reaction is harnessed

43
00:07:55,560 --> 00:08:02,600
to produce steam to turn turbines to generate electricity.

44
00:08:03,959 --> 00:08:07,800
The Atomic Energy Commission has sponsored the design and development of

45
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:14,680
a number of different types of power reactors to gain broad experience for future large-scale development.

46
00:08:21,400 --> 00:08:27,080
BONUS is an outgrowth of a power reactor concept that uses water as the moderator,

47
00:08:27,080 --> 00:08:28,680
reflector, and coolant.

48
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:37,320
That is, the steam produced in this central boiler region at a temperature of 540 degrees

49
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:42,540
Fahrenheit is passed through special super heater fuel elements located on

50
00:08:42,540 --> 00:08:48,820
the periphery of the core. No auxiliary heating is necessary.

51
00:08:53,379 --> 00:08:58,580
The superheated steam flows out of the reactor core at 900 degrees Fahrenheit

52
00:08:58,580 --> 00:09:04,340
and 850 pounds per square inch. Temperatures and pressures for most

53
00:09:04,340 --> 00:09:18,040
efficient use in the latest types of turbo generating equipment.

54
00:09:18,039 --> 00:09:25,039
It's February 1963, and the bonus pressure vessel has reached the harbor of San Juan.

55
00:09:48,039 --> 00:09:55,039
Now another part of the job begins, to move this 61 ton object across the length of the

56
00:09:56,599 --> 00:10:03,599
island without a scratch or dent to its precisely finished features.

57
00:10:48,039 --> 00:11:15,620
At Punta Iguera, the containment shell has been completed, a gas-tight building constructed

58
00:11:15,620 --> 00:11:21,299
to hold internal pressures of five pounds to the square inch.

59
00:11:21,299 --> 00:11:29,060
It will house all of the reactor and generating facilities.

60
00:11:29,060 --> 00:11:33,039
The turbo generator has been installed by the water resources authority.

61
00:11:33,039 --> 00:11:40,419
The space beyond awaits the pressure vessel.

62
00:11:40,419 --> 00:11:45,419
Now, like the key piece in a giant jigsaw puzzle, it moves into place.

63
00:12:10,419 --> 00:12:33,419
Once the pressure vessel is in position, it will be wrapped and embedded in a 10-foot

64
00:12:33,419 --> 00:12:38,179
shield of steel, water, and concrete.

65
00:12:38,179 --> 00:12:43,319
Meanwhile, the innumerable connections are being completed.

66
00:12:43,319 --> 00:12:47,459
Steam outlets from the superheaters,

67
00:12:47,459 --> 00:12:51,360
water recirculation piping, and all

68
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:54,459
of the other facilities that will feed and cool,

69
00:12:54,459 --> 00:12:58,339
control, and safeguard the reactor.

70
00:12:58,340 --> 00:13:01,620
the instruments that will analyze its moods and responses.

71
00:13:06,060 --> 00:13:09,680
Into the waiting pressure vessel will go the internals,

72
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:13,160
the core structure that holds the uranium fuel assemblies

73
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:19,019
amid a torrent of water, 9,000 gallons per minute.

74
00:13:19,019 --> 00:13:26,139
Once installed inside the pressure vessel, the core structure will not be removed.

75
00:13:26,139 --> 00:13:29,819
This is the last look, the final inspection.

76
00:13:32,699 --> 00:13:36,460
Impurities cannot be tolerated in a reactor system.

77
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:40,220
At this stage of installation, the requirement for cleanliness,

78
00:13:40,220 --> 00:13:43,419
always rigorous, becomes absolute.

79
00:13:43,420 --> 00:14:01,040
Because the bonus reactor is intended to fill a specific need, illuminating one area in

80
00:14:01,040 --> 00:14:07,220
research and development, it differs from every other reactor in its design, its engineering

81
00:14:07,220 --> 00:14:11,440
and construction.

82
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:18,280
Of the $18 million being expended by AEC on bonus, a sizable amount must go into research

83
00:14:18,280 --> 00:14:30,260
and development.

84
00:14:30,260 --> 00:14:36,600
Each of AEC's reactor projects imposes demands upon the designer and engineer that are different

85
00:14:36,600 --> 00:14:38,820
and difficult.

86
00:14:38,820 --> 00:14:50,460
that must be solved each time from the origins of their complexity.

87
00:14:50,460 --> 00:14:57,020
Beside technological know-how, what else is going into the building a bonus?

88
00:14:57,020 --> 00:15:03,340
There are thousands of hours of plain, hard physical labor, work that differs from routine

89
00:15:03,340 --> 00:15:07,540
by the need to meet exacting standards at every step.

90
00:15:25,540 --> 00:15:29,540
There is the slow increase in knowledge that comes from one day to the next,

91
00:15:29,740 --> 00:15:31,840
from one project to the next.

92
00:15:31,840 --> 00:15:38,360
The growth of experience in the ways of harnessing and handling this new source of power safely.

93
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:56,960
And, there is the unexpected setback, breaking abruptly into the schedule.

94
00:15:56,960 --> 00:16:00,620
This time, it's one of the recirculating water pumps.

95
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:07,620
This whole phase of installation comes to a halt as the mechanics work intently to fix it.

96
00:16:20,840 --> 00:16:23,460
Estimated delay, three days.

97
00:16:24,160 --> 00:16:27,240
Actual recorded delay, five hours.

98
00:16:31,840 --> 00:16:35,940
Slowly, in all of its complexity, the reactor takes form.

99
00:16:40,399 --> 00:16:43,220
These are control rod drive units.

100
00:16:45,300 --> 00:16:48,720
They will power the two types of control rods

101
00:16:48,720 --> 00:16:51,980
whose movements start and stop the chain reaction

102
00:16:51,980 --> 00:16:54,320
and maintain safe operation.

103
00:17:01,840 --> 00:17:12,460
They must transmit the finest adjustment or drop instantly into the core when the scram

104
00:17:12,460 --> 00:17:21,779
button is pushed to shut down the reactor.

105
00:17:21,779 --> 00:17:27,100
Now bonus is being subjected to continuous cycles of testing as components are checked

106
00:17:27,099 --> 00:17:44,619
against components, systems against systems, and final adjustments completed.

107
00:17:44,619 --> 00:17:50,279
Finally the reactor, complete and functional, is ready to receive its nuclear fuel, fabricated

108
00:17:50,279 --> 00:17:56,439
by Combustion Engineering.

109
00:17:56,440 --> 00:18:10,799
The finely wrought fuel assemblies, 96 of them, contain a total of 4 1⁄2 tons of uranium.

110
00:18:10,799 --> 00:18:19,380
One by one they're lowered into place deep within the core structure.

111
00:18:19,380 --> 00:18:44,860
Under the boiler section goes 64 enriched uranium oxide clad with zircaloy II.

112
00:18:44,860 --> 00:18:49,400
For the super heater section, 32 fuel assemblies are provided.

113
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:55,620
They contain enriched uranium oxide clad within canal, inserted within stainless steel pressure

114
00:18:55,620 --> 00:19:19,760
tubes for the passage of steam.

115
00:19:19,759 --> 00:19:25,660
The evening of April 13th 1964 brings a culmination.

116
00:19:25,660 --> 00:19:28,500
It's called the initial criticality test.

117
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:37,279
The moment when the reactor is to control nuclear energy for the first time.

118
00:19:37,279 --> 00:19:39,099
Everyone is busy tonight.

119
00:19:39,099 --> 00:19:43,579
The reactor operators at the controls, the other members of the staff double checking

120
00:19:43,579 --> 00:19:48,960
the data that feeds off the instrument panels.

121
00:19:48,960 --> 00:20:04,159
2033 hours, April 13th, 1964.

122
00:20:04,159 --> 00:20:09,539
In the long succession of events that marks any major construction project, this is one

123
00:20:09,539 --> 00:20:14,579
of the peaks when these men can look back over their work and look forward

124
00:20:14,579 --> 00:20:19,740
into the future and find both of them good.

125
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:36,420
BONUS is producing power under the operation of these staff members of the

126
00:20:36,420 --> 00:20:43,420
Water Resources Authority. They were trained at the AEC's Puerto Rico Nuclear Center and

127
00:20:43,460 --> 00:20:50,460
other AEC sites. AEC is paying the costs of operation while the Water Resources Authority

128
00:20:54,380 --> 00:21:01,380
is purchasing the steam produced by the reactor from AEC. Then, out of this cooperation, power

129
00:21:01,380 --> 00:21:08,560
Then, out of this cooperation, power from BONUS is moving across the green hills to

130
00:21:08,560 --> 00:21:24,360
the cities and farms and factories of Puerto Rico.

131
00:21:24,360 --> 00:21:31,140
The knowledge and practical experience obtained through BONUS is helping bring power, cheap,

132
00:21:31,140 --> 00:21:34,140
abundant power, to many parts of the world.
